=== ffplay ===
DESCRIPTION ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Simple media player


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ffplay [options] input_file


POSITIONALS (1) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  input_file


FLAGS (11) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Main options
-L                       show license
-h topic                 show help

AVCodecContext AVOptions ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
    -flags flags         (default 0)
                           values:
                             unaligned       .D.V....... allow decoders to
                                             produce unaligned output
                             gray            ED.V....... only decode/encode
                                             grayscale
                             low_delay       ED.V....... force low delay
                             bitexact        ED.VAS..... use only bitexact
                                             functions (except (I)DCT)
                             output_corrupt  .D.V....... Output even
                                             potentially corrupted frames
                             drop_changed    .D.VA.....P Drop frames whose
                                             parameters differ from first
                                             decoded frame

Libdc1394 indev AVOptions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
    -video_size string   A string describing frame size, such as 640x480 or
                         hd720. (default "qvga")
    -pixel_format string (default "uyvy422")
    -framerate string    (default "ntsc")

AVFilter AVOptions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    thread_type flags    Allowed thread types (default slice)
                           values:
                             slice  ..F........
    enable string        set enable expression
    threads int          Allowed number of threads (from 0 to INT_MAX)
                         (default 0)
    extra_hw_frames int  Number of extra hardware frames to allocate for the
                         user (from -1 to INT_MAX) (default -1)

Abench AVOptions ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    action int           set action (from 0 to 1) (default start)
                           values:
                             start  0 ..F.A...... start timer
                             stop   1 ..F.A...... stop timer
